{"role":"tool","content":"[subagent Find BAFTA 2019 game winner · 25 tool uses]\nI'll search for this information using multiple approaches simultaneouslyBoth tools seem to have encountered issues. Let me retry the searches.Let me try the webfetch approach and also check if the screenshot tool mightWeb tools appear to be restricted. Let me use bash to fetch the informationLet me try checking the project for any relevant files and attempt different search approaches\nLet me retry the search and fetch tools nowLet me check what's available in the working directory and try alternative approaches.Let me try once more with different tool invocations:Unfortunately, the external tools (websearch, webfetch, bash) are all returning permission errors, so I can't perform live verification. However, based on my knowledge of the award:\n\n---\n\n**The British Academy Games Award for Best Game (2019 ceremony):**\n\n- **Winner:** **God of War**\n- **Release Date:** **April 20, 2018**\n- **Developer:** Santa Monica Studio\n- **Publisher:** Sony Interactive Entertainment\n\nThe **15th British Academy Game Awards** ceremony took place on **April 2, 2019** at the Troxy in London. *God of War* (2018) won the top prize of **Best Game**, along with several other BAFTAs that evening (including Narrative, Game Design, and Audio Achievement). The game's release on April 20, 2018, placed it squarely in the eligibility period for the 2019 ceremony.\n\n---\n\n**To verify:** You can confirm this by checking the Wikipedia page for the [15th British Academy Game Awards](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/15th_British_Academy_Game_Awards) or the [British Academy Game Awards](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Academy_Game_Awards) page.\n\n**Summary:** *God of War* (released April 20, 2018) won the BAFTA Games Award for Best Game at the 2019 ceremony.","toolCallId":"call_5b704e36f9234f09838ce60e","name":"task"}
