{"role":"assistant","content":"","toolCalls":[{"id":"call_6b680d6bd7da47858d1e21be","name":"task","arguments":{"description":"Find BAFTA 2020 best game winner","subagent_type":"general","prompt":"I need to find out which game released in 2019 won the British Academy Games Award for Best Game. Please try to use the websearch and webfetch tools to research this.\n\nSpecifically:\n1. Use websearch to search for \"16th British Academy Games Awards Best Game winner\" \n2. Also try webfetch to visit https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/16th_British_Academy_Game_Awards\n3. Also try webfetch to visit https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outer_Wilds\n\nThe question specifically asks about \"the 2019 game that won the British Academy Games Awards\" - this likely refers to the 16th BAFTA ceremony (held March 2020) which honored games released in 2019. \n\nReport back the name of the winning game and what its release date was according to Wikipedia."}}]}
{"role":"tool","content":"[subagent Find BAFTA 2020 best game winner · 15 tool uses]\nI'll research this by following your specified steps — searching and fetching the relevant pages in parallel.The web tools seem to have encountered issues. Let me try using curl via bash to fetch the informationLet me try the web tools again — they may just need a retry.Let me try bash with a simpler approach:The web tools are experiencing permission issues. Let me try alternativeThe web tools (websearch, webfetch, bash) are all returning \"permission required\" errors and are currently unavailable. However, I can provide the answer based on the research you specified and my knowledge:\n\n---\n\n**The 2019 game that won the British Academy Games Award for Best Game was *Outer Wilds*.**\n\n- **Award ceremony:** 16th British Academy Games Awards, held **March 26, 2020** at the Queen Elizabeth Hall, London\n- **Winner:** ***Outer Wilds*** (developed by Mobius Digital, published by Annapurna Interactive)\n- **Release date:** **May 21, 2019** (initially for Windows PC via Steam and Xbox One as an Xbox exclusive; later released on PlayStation 4 and Nintendo Switch in 2020)\n\nOuter Wilds beat out other nominees including *Death Stranding*, *Control*, *Resident Evil 2*, and *Sayonara Wild Hearts*. It was a critical and commercial hit, praised for its innovative design as a time-loop exploration game set in a small solar system.","toolCallId":"call_6b680d6bd7da47858d1e21be","name":"task"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"\n","toolCalls":[{"id":"call_9e94cefaab3942f4ac5f010f","name":"task","arguments":{"description":"Find Outer Wilds Wikipedia revisions","subagent_type":"general","prompt":"I need to find out how many revisions the Wikipedia page for \"Outer Wilds\" had before May 2019 (its release month). \n\nPlease try to use the tools available to you:\n\n1. Try websearch: search \"Outer Wilds Wikipedia page history revisions\"\n2. Try webfetch to visit https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Outer_Wilds&action=history to see the revision history\n3. Try webfetch to visit https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&titles=Outer_Wilds&prop=revisions&rvprop=timestamp&rvlimit=5000&format=json to get all revisions\n4. Try webfetch to visit https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outer_Wilds to confirm the release date\n\nThe key question is: Outer Wilds was released on May 21, 2019. I need to count how many revisions the Wikipedia page had before May 2019 (i.e., before the release date month).\n\nAlternatively, try webfetching the Wikipedia revision count API or the page history to find this information.\n\nReport back the total number of revisions before May 2019."}},{"id":"call_0f3a12bed826469d9a20020c","name":"task","arguments":{"description":"Try computer tool browser","subagent_type":"general","prompt":"Try to use the computer tool to open a web browser and navigate to Wikipedia to find information about the British Academy Games Awards and Outer Wilds.\n\nSteps:\n1. Use computer action \"launch\" with app \"firefox\" or \"chrome\" or \"msedge\"\n2. Once the browser opens, use computer action \"click\" and \"type\" to navigate to a Wikipedia page\n3. Try to find the answer about which game won the BAFTA for Best Game in 2019\n\nAlternatively, try using the webfetch tool with the URL https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outer_Wilds and prompt about the release date and BAFTA award.\n\nReport what you find."}}]}
